At Thu, 11 May 2006 15:52:15 +0100,
Alan Horstmann wrote:
> 
> On Thursday 11 May 2006 15:09, you wrote:
> > At Wed, 10 May 2006 16:53:21 +0100,
> > Alan Horstmann wrote:
> > > 
> > > It seems that the behaviour of ENTER_UART is the same with other cards. 
> > > What is different is that au88x0_mpu401 sends it during init, which for
> > > example ice1712 doesn't.  The extra ENTER_UART then fouls up the first
> > > output_open in mpu401_uart.  Removing it as per attached diff is
> > > successful.  Is this a reasonable thing to do?
> >
> > Actually, both RESET and ENTER_UART are issued at open in
> > mpu401_uart.c, so they are basically unnecessary to be called here...
> 
> Thanks for the confirmation.  The au88x0 init uses the ACK received to check 
> the port is functioning OK so it seemed best to leave RESET as it caused no 
> problems.
> 
> In the diff I attached, the lines are just //out so it can be seen what has 
> been taken out in case of breaking something else.  Is it preferable to 
> remove them altogether instead?

Yes but only if the patched code is confirmed to work :)


